USB3 (and probably 2) was disabled at some point, but re-enabled when I
flashed the bios and had to reconfigure everything.

Both boot fast if no USB is connected.

If I connect USB devices during boot, the crap EUFI bios takes
conciderably longer than without. A complaint to asus on the newegg
'forums' and they said 'uefi is slow' (I dind't attribute that to the
USB at that point).

Booting 32bit kernel everything seems to work just fine. With and
without USB devices connected.

On a 64bit kernel, with USB devices connected, it boots at normal speed,
but 'hangs' when USB is being initialized, which slows down boot to take
minutes. So no, it doesn't boot slowly per say, just when USB inits and
probes the bus, it waits for that/hangs.

lsusb hangs long times too when devices are attached.


What 2 dmesg logs would you like? 64bit with and without devices
attached? I attach a USB device after the kernel booted, to spawn the
same (iirc) error message as when it boots (which was included before).

In any case I have attached a 64bit boot log with an USB stick connected,
if that is what you ment.



